.TH MMAP_READ_FD_RANGE 3
.SH NAME
mmap_read_fd_range \- create a partial shared, read-only mapping of a file descriptor
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include "mmap.h"
.PP
.BI "char* mmap_read_fd_range(fd_type " fd ", size_t* " size ", size_t " offset ", size_t " len ");"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mmap_read_fd_range
maps a range of
.I len
bytes starting at
.I offset
from the file descriptor
.I fd
into memory as a shared, read-only mapping.
The actual number of bytes mapped is stored in
.I size
(which will be the lesser of
.I len
or the file size).
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns a pointer to the mapped memory on success, or NULL on failure.